# What ran before a step in a loop is every call of the loop, whichever stands first (#329): a later round runs after
# every call of the one before. `main` sets the drafts up, and each round keeps its report on the shelf and then opens
# the shelf on `out`. The first round keeps it on the drafts; every later round keeps it on the shelf the round before
# opened. So `write` under `keep_report` writes the report in both folders: the drafts' set-up ran before the loop, and
# `open_shelf` ran before it in the round before, although it stands after it in the body.

route rounds.main
step main/open_drafts
step main/open_drafts/Shelf()
step main/Shelf.keep_report
step main/Shelf.keep_report/write
step main/open_shelf
step main/open_shelf/Shelf()

line entry > main call
line main/open_drafts/Shelf() > Shelf@main/open_drafts/Shelf() value
line Shelf@main/open_drafts/Shelf() > main/open_drafts value
line main/open_drafts > Shelf·shelf@main/open_drafts value
line main/open_shelf/Shelf() > Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() value
line Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() > main/open_shelf value
line main/open_shelf > Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf value
line Shelf·shelf@main/open_drafts > main/Shelf.keep_report/write value     # the first round: `write(self.root / ..)`
known #354 line Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf > main/Shelf.keep_report/write value     # every later round, on the shelf opened
line main/Shelf.keep_report/write > File(drafts/report.txt) own
line main/Shelf.keep_report/write > File(out/report.txt) own

home Shelf@main/open_drafts/Shelf() main/open_drafts
home Shelf·shelf@main/open_drafts main
home Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() main/open_shelf
home Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf main

side entry left
side File(drafts/report.txt) right
side File(out/report.txt) right
